<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA OFFERS 6.9 BLN LEVS 119-DAY T-BILLS OCT 21.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA OFFERS 6.9 BLN LEVS 119-DAY T-BILLS OCT 21.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 6.9 billion levs of 119-day floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Monday, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, a BNB statement said.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3019896029</p>
<p> Type		   Floater coupon</p>
<p> Par value	    6.9 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	 October 21, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   October 23, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	February 19, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
